Struct Definition vs. Instantiation
    Struct Definition
        : Defines a template or blueprint for what data a struct will contain. No memory is allocated; it only describes the structure.
    Struct Instantiation
        : Creates an actual variable of that struct type, which reserves memory for all data members.

