Initialization Order
    : Consider the following struct:
        struct Point
        {
            int x;
            int y;
            char label;
        };
    a) If you initialize a Point variable with struct Point p1 = {5, 10, 'A'};
    which value is assigned to which data member? Why is order important? 
        5 is assigned to x (first data member)
        10 is assigned to y (second data member)
        'A' is assigned to label (third data member)
        Order is important because values are assigned to data members in the order they are declared in the struct definition. 
        If the order is wrong, data will be assigned to the wrong fields.
